Two films can look the same on your car and still perform very differently. Many shops sell both TPU and TPH. Because the material decides how long the protection lasts, it pays to check first. Here is how to identify TPU and TPH PPF without any special tools.
Which Materials Are Used in PPF?
Most paint protection film falls into three groups: TPU, TPH, and older PVC. TPU (thermoplastic polyurethane) is the best grade. TPH is a hybrid that costs less, and sources describe it differently. These are the basics you need.
TPU vs TPH PPF for Cars: How They Differ
TPU: Flexible, self-healing, clear for years, and longer lasting
TPH: Less elastic, limited healing, can yellow or crack, and cheaper
The quality gap is hard to judge on day one. It appears with time.
