FAQs
What is the best way to know if PPF is TPU or TPH? Check your invoice, warranty card, and brand, then verify with the maker. TPU stretches smoothly and heals light scratches, while TPH is stiffer and heals less.
Can TPH PPF recover from scratches? Usually not well. TPU is known for heat-based healing, and TPH tends to have limited or none.
Does TPU beat TPH every time? For most owners, it does. It is more flexible, clearer, and longer lasting, though TPH may suit a tight budget or short-term use.
What are the warning signs of weak PPF? Look for no brand, a very low price, a hazy or yellow tint, and a stiff feel. A missing self-heal effect or a short warranty is also a bad sign.
Can the installer hand me a sample? Yes, a good one should. They should also show the roll label and data sheet, and refusing is a warning sign.
How many years can TPU PPF last? Quality TPU can last up to 10 years with proper installation and care. Weather, driving conditions, and upkeep all affect it.
